{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Temporal Difference \u2014 Q-Learning & SARSA Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: SARSA on \u03b5-greedy policy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sarsa(env, episodes, alpha=0.1, gamma=0.99, epsilon=0.1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    Q = defaultdict(lambda: {a: 0.0 for a in ACTIONS})"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def choose(s):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if random() < epsilon:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return choice(ACTIONS)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return max(Q[s], key=Q[s].get)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(episodes):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        s = env.reset()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        a = choose(s)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        while True:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            s_next, r, done = env.step(s, a)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            a_next = choose(s_next) if not done else None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            target = r + (gamma * Q[s_next][a_next] if not done else 0.0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            Q[s][a] += alpha * (target - Q[s][a])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if done:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                break"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            s, a = s_next, a_next"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return Q"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Eight lines. The *only* difference from Q-learning is the target line."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Q-learning"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def q_learning(env, episodes, alpha=0.1, gamma=0.99, epsilon=0.1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    Q = defaultdict(lambda: {a: 0.0 for a in ACTIONS})"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(episodes):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        s = env.reset()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        while True:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            a = choose(s, Q, epsilon)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            s_next, r, done = env.step(s, a)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            target = r + (gamma * max(Q[s_next].values()) if not done else 0.0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            Q[s][a] += alpha * (target - Q[s][a])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if done:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                break"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            s = s_next"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return Q"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The `max` decouples target from behavior. That one symbol is the difference between on-policy and off-policy."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: learning curves"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Track mean return per 100 episodes. Q-learning converges faster on simple deterministic GridWorld; SARSA is more conservative on cliff-walking. On the 4\u00d74 GridWorld in `code/main.py`, both are near-optimal after ~2,000 episodes with `\u03b1=0.1, \u03b5=0.1`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: compare to DP truth"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run value iteration (Lesson 02) to get `Q*`. Check `max_{s,a} |Q_learned(s,a) - Q*(s,a)|`. A healthy tabular TD agent lands within `~0.5` on the 4\u00d74 GridWorld after 10,000 episodes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Implement Q-learning and SARSA on the 4\u00d74 GridWorld. Plot learning curves (mean return per 100 episodes) for 2,000 episodes. Who converges faster?\n2. **Medium.** Build a cliff-walking environment (4\u00d712, last row is the cliff with reward -100 and reset to start). Compare Q-learning and SARSA final policies. Screenshot the paths each takes. Which is closer to the cliff?\n3. **Hard.** Implement Double Q-learning. On a noisy-reward GridWorld (Gaussian noise \u03c3=5 added to per-step reward), show Q-learning overestimates `V*(0,0)` by a meaningful amount while Double Q-learning does not."
      ]
    }
